WEBVTT

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.350
<i>Maybe I got here too early.</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.650
<i>Guess I'll go check out 
study guides for Mikage.</i>

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.490
<b>Fall Chapter Episode 11
Over and Over Again</b>

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.460
Hey, isn't that Hachiken?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.170
Where?

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.140
That guy wearing glasses over there.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.970
Wasn't he skinnier?

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:04.160
Poincaré

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:58.700
You gonna talk to him?

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.010
Eh, dunno.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:04.140
He was such a downer around graduation, 
 so it wasn't easy to talk to him.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:05.400
You go talk to him.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.870
We can't see his face, though.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:08.870
Poincaré

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.260
It's Hachiken, after all.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.560
Long time no see!

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.820
Oh, been a while.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.380
You're at an agricultural 
high school, right?

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.440
What's it like?

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.740
Well, it's okay.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.910
Are you raising cows?

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:20.820
Does manure smell?

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:21.740
What do you study?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.510
Hey, did you bulk up a bit?

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.420
Do you get to eat all the meat you want?

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:25.030
What about veggies?

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.340
Oh, they're great when 
they're freshly picked.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.690
I've raised a pig and made him into bacon.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.480
I've made pizza for everyone to eat, too.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:32.840
Whoa!

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.240
Do students have to till the fields by hand?

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:36.700
No way, they've gotta use machines.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.230
But how can they drive 
them without a license?

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:39.730
I can drive a tractor.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:40.800
Whoa!

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.820
Right!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.590
I was imagining something more pastoral.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:44.420
You don't have horses, either?

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:45.130
No way!

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.560
Farm tools are all modernized and stuff!

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.810
No one's riding horses around.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.790
I can... ride horses, too.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.270
Whoa!

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:54.250
You can make food, drive machines, 
and ride animals?

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:55.530
What's up with that?

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.480
I'm jealous!

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.690
Nah, my classmates there say

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.490
they're jealous of people who're good 
at studying and can get good grades...

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.320
I guess the grass is always 
greener on the other side.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.520
Hachiken, what's your contact info right now?

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.180
Tell me, too.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.330
Me, too.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.330
Oh, sure.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.780
Oh, I saw you looking at study guides.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:11.960
Did you figure out which 
school you want to get into?

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.420
Oh, it's not for me.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.200
I'm helping a friend study
 for college entrance exams.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.860
You're studying with a grimy 
agricultural high school dude?

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:20.070
Sounds like a drag.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.050
Nah, not at all.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.510
My friend's a girl.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.880
Take that, human genome sequence!

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.210
Pi to a hundred thousand digits!

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:29.570
English sex slang dictionary!

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.630
Incredible, but I can't use those!

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.280
See you!

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:39.210
Man, that was a shocker.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:42.030
I didn't think I'd see guys 
from junior high here.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.730
<i>But I'm relieved...</i>

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.050
<i>I had a normal conversation with them.</i>

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.720
Hachiken's changed a lot.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.710
Yeah.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.180
I'm back.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.770
<i>No one's home?</i>

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.730
<b>Stocks 101</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
Oh, there they are!

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.030
Bro's handwriting sucks.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.520
I can't read this!

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.480
Whatever.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.200
I'll just take my time deciphering 
them after I get back.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.570
I'll just leave a note...

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.840
Here you go!

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:48.100
I've been cooking for two for so long

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.810
that I forgot how to adjust
 the amount of ingredients.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.860
Thanks for the food...

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.190
It's delicious.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:04:59.830
What?

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:00.360
Huh?

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:05.700
It just seems like such a long time
 since you ate my cooking and said it was good.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.070
<i>Oh, I guess I blurted it out.</i>

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:11.680
Dad won't ever comment on the 
taste either, so it's boring.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:12.690
It's fine.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.290
That's not what I mean.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.550
I have no complaints.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:16.490
Um...

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:20.750
Your parents made sure you guys 
had good food growing up.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.600
<i>Made sure...</i>

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:34.360
Um, so...

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.200
Do we have any debt?

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.750
Where'd that unpleasant talk come from?

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.460
Well, my friend's place...

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.610
They had to shut down their 
business because of debt,

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.450
and then he had
to withdraw from school, too.

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:48.950
Oh, my...

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.230
We have savings.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:52.030
Don't worry about money.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.120
What if I said I want to go to college?

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.010
You decided where you want to go?

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:59.990
No, that's not it...

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:02.130
We have enough saved up 
for your tuition, too.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.630
Can you afford to waste your time 
thinking about things like that?

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:07.520
Focus on studying.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:13.470
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.280
<i>Calm down...</i>

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.420
<i>Try to understand, right?</i>

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.930
I can see where you're coming from.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:25.860
I've recently begun to see that.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.490
My friend decided she wants 
a different future for herself,

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:33.690
but that means going to college 
which she hadn't previously planned on.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:38.100
Her dream job is to work 
in the Ban'ei stables,

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.670
but the industry's tough right now.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.270
Even if she tries to get a 
different job with horses,

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:46.990
working at places like JRA 
requires a college degree.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:50.390
Even if she has a dream, it's like...

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:53.210
Kind of like a car missing a wheel.

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:55.510
She can't move forward, unless 
she gets the other wheel.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:59.520
That wheel that's offsetting 
the dream might be suitability

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.100
or money...

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:02.780
and all kinds of other things,

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:06.360
but what my friend needs
 right now is good grades.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.740
You came to borrow Shingo's 
notes for that friend?

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:12.790
Yeah...

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:16.500
The way things are, getting into the college 
she's thinking about is a long shot.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.790
I'm trying to fix that.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.910
I'm helping her study.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:24.260
I thought I should, if there's 
anything I can help her learn...

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.920
You're saying that someone 
who failed in his studies

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.110
can help someone else with theirs?

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:43.440
So, someone who failed...

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:47.600
Someone who failed once can't 
do anything else after that?

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:51.700
One failure and everything's 
a done deal after that?

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.390
That's almost like being livestock.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.970
One little illness, one little injury...

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:03.460
If their productivity goes down, 
off they go to the slaughterhouse.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.130
That's just like being livestock!

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.140
No, even livestock don't

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:11.920
aren't killed so easily, 
if their owner doesn't allow it.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.570
Even horses doing show jumps

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:17.430
get another chance if
 they fail the first time!

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.430
Am I less than livestock?

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.330
I'm leaving.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.370
Thanks for the food!

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:48.630
That boy dutifully cleared 
the dishes from the table.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.540
<b>Thank you. 
 -Mikage</b>

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.560
<i>My, this is from a girl, isn't it?</i>

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:57.880
<i>And these must be from boys.</i>

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:04.430
<i>Come to think of it, I don't even 
know what Yuugo's doing at school...</i>

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.060
<i>I forgot all my presents there...</i>

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:14.270
<i>I wish I could've eaten the 
fresh cheese from Mikage!</i>

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.530
<b>Cafeteria</b>

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.380
Progress is slow...

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:20.970
Sorry.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:23.220
Oh, it's not your fault.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.600
My teaching method must be bad...

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:26.750
That's not true!

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.930
Hachiken-kun?

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:31.480
Oh, sorry.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.210
I was just thinking of what I should do.

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:37.270
Yeah, I'll manage something, so don't worry.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:39.760
Just keep studying the 
way you've been, Mikage.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.270
<i>Talk about messy handwriting...</i>

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.380
<i>Am I even going to be able to decipher this?</i>

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.520
<i>Crap...</i>

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:51.730
<i>At this rate, I won't be able to 
get Mikage into her first choice.</i>

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.150
Damn it!

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.400
Just you wait...

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:04.090
One day of suspension for every broken egg...

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:05.750
You were joking, right, sensei?!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.610
I told you!

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.710
You are slaves to the livestock!

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:14.040
I wonder why it grates me less 
to be told up front

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.420
that I'm worth less than livestock.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.890
Wow, your dad said something like that?

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.990
Your dad's scary.

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:24.890
Yeah, he's awful.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:27.930
It felt like he was telling me 
that someone who failed once

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.520
doesn't even have the right to try a second time.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:31.370
Right.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:34.200
Well, I can see where your 
father is coming from.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:34.740
What?!

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.990
You're also saying
 there's no failure allowed?

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.740
Everyone fails.

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.790
But in this case,

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:45.010
you were the one who failed the entrance exam
 in the first place, right, Hachiken?

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.200
You're making Aki take on the second attempt.

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:49.580
I'm sure you understand already,

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:54.460
but don't weigh Aki down just because
 you want to salvage your own pride.

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:59.250
Help her study without 
involving your pride at all.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:01.100
Tamako, that was harsh.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:01.950
Really?

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.470
It's not like I want anyone's 
dream to be broken.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.380
I want hers to come true 
in the best way possible.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.020
<i>I'd totally forgotten about it...</i>

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:10.110
<i>It's not so that I get to jump...</i>

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.160
<i>It's so that Mikage can jump!</i>

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:13.890
<i>Idiot!</i>

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:16.880
<i>You put yourself on the line 
to understand that before!</i>

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:18.580
Tamako!

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:19.190
Hit me—

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:19.760
Sure.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.870
Can't you at least try 
to act a little conflicted...

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.650
or be less blasé about it?

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:28.700
I don't have time to deal
 with teenage boy drama.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.160
Mikage!

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.300
Oh, Hachiken, your mom—

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:37.590
Mikage, hit me—

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.070
Hachiken-kun!

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:44.670
I have to apologize to you.

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:45.760
Yuugo, are you okay?!

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:47.600
Huh?!

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.480
Mom! Why are you here?

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:53.020
I don't know anything 
about your high school,

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.360
so I wondered what your life here was like...

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.060
This must be out of your comfort zone, 
but you seem to be trying hard.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:03.360
I'm glad to see you have a lot of friends.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.410
Oh, the presents you brought 
were delicious, too.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:07.300
Your friends also made the 
presents you left behind, right?

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:10.200
Yeah, well... Yeah.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:15.170
Oh, the yogurt in the bottle was really good!

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.780
Do they sell that here?

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.500
Sorry.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:20.160
What?

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.800
No, really. Sorry.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.850
Okay, this foot next.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.960
Horses are very obedient, aren't they?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:41.890
No, it's only because Hachiken-kun is very 
responsible about taking care of them.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:45.990
Okay! Done!

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:49.460
Yo, Hachi.

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:52.000
Oh, you guys still have practicum?

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.540
It looks like it's going to snow, 
so there's a lot to put away...

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:57.890
My mom.

00:12:57.890 --> 00:12:59.500
Thank you for looking after my son.

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.960
Hachi's mom?

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:02.230
Nice to meet you.

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.480
I'm the principal.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:04.070
Huh?!

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.890
Oh, thank you for taking care of my son!

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.900
That'll be 250 yen.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:12.600
Thanks.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:15.060
Wow, they're so cheap!

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.350
No way...

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.700
So much that's so fresh at such prices...

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:19.920
I'm about to clear out,

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.690
so I can give you a bigger discount.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:24.460
But I still have to go home to Sapporo,

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:25.700
and they'll be heavy...

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:26.900
Too bad!

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:27.780
If that's the case...

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.530
...why not have them here?

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.160
Hey, Beppu?

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.050
Are you free?

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:34.250
<i>Here we go again...</i>

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:38.980
We can only make simple 
dishes, but here you go!

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.460
Wow!

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:42.460
You don't flip the 
shiitake mushrooms over,

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:45.880
but wait until you see beads 
of water form on the "gills."

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.340
Sprinkle with salt, and here you go!

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:48.340
Huh?!

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.710
It should be with lemon juice and soy sauce!

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:50.770
What?! Should be shichimi!

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:51.550
Ginger soy sauce!

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:54.110
It's not bad with mayonnaise, soy sauce, 
chili pepper when you wash it down with beer!

00:13:54.110 --> 00:13:55.350
I heard "beer."

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:57.600
I brought some all-natural bacon!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.010
What's this yummy smell?

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:03.360
Piping hot rice!

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.910
Let's make raclette with potatoes!

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:07.560
<b>Reserve</b>

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.570
What?!

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.550
Yum!

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:15.310
It's all delicious!

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:19.690
It's the only thing I've 
been saying for a while.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:21.390
Sorry if I'm being noisy.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.250
We want to hear more!

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:27.270
Why is this spinach so sweet?

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:30.530
Spinach has a high tolerance for frost.

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:32.600
We deliberately expose them to the cold.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.770
Why don't they get damaged by the frost?

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.350
They store sugars in their leaves.

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:40.630
Oh, so the sugars lower the freezing point.

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:41.330
What?

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.230
A special move?

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:44.210
Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius,

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.460
but sugar water doesn't 
freeze at that temperature.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:47.490
Why not?

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:51.390
When water freezes, the water molecules 
stick to each other to form ice.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:56.740
But in sugar water, the dissolved sugar
 molecules make that process harder.

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:57.500
Oh...

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.880
Oh, Nishikawa and Beppu here 
made the pickles and the natto.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.770
Oh, thank you for making them!

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.730
Oh, I made the men's bath yog—

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:11.310
I was shocked by how tasty they were!

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:12.550
Really?

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:16.090
It's really motivating to hear someone say
 they enjoy your food.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:17.110
Right!

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:21.270
I try harder when I get good 
feedback on my own cooking.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.270
Come to think of it, Hachiken-kun,

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.140
didn't you say you had to 
apologize to me about something?

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.060
Oh...

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.410
Tamako said something that made me realize...

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:36.030
that my motivation to get you into college

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:38.700
might have at least partly come from 
wanting to rebel against my dad...

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.250
So, I'm really sorry!

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.360
That's it?

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:43.630
"That's it"?

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:48.820
I was about to confuse my pride
 with your entrance exam.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.570
Well, I don't blame you.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:53.140
You went through a lot, after all.

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:56.040
So you'll... forgive me?

00:15:56.040 --> 00:16:00.010
Forgive you? It's not like 
you hurt me or anything.

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:02.480
You help me study every day.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:03.770
What a relief!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:06.380
Oh, I'm relieved, too!

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:07.690
Huh? About what?

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:13.240
Well, you always seem so tense 
when you're studying with me, so...

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.400
I thought you hated me 
because I was so dumb—

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.620
No, no, never!

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.250
No matter what, I... I...

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:28.750
Well, Hachiken?

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:28.750
Stop!

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:31.850
Hachiken, how's the teen spirit spice mix?!

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:35.080
Ookawa-senpai, did you find a job?

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.180
Hachiken, your mouth is bright red!

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:37.180
I'm glad I came.

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:40.100
I had no idea...

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:42.890
No, maybe I just didn't try.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:50.860
I'm glad I got to talk with you today, too.

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:53.500
It's the same with every student,

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:56.320
but it's reassuring to meet their parents.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.020
Well, you know.

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:02.870
It's like seeing a photo of farmers on the 
packaging of crops and feeling reassured.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.760
You get a sense of where they came from.

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:05.840
Right?!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.290
Don't show up unannounced.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:15.280
Unannounced?

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:17.220
Look who's talking.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:22.890
I was so surprised.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:26.340
When you talked back to your father.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.720
You were always so quiet at home.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:32.740
Yeah, I'm a wimp.

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.540
Dad lands heavy punches with his logic, too.

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:37.790
I'm not as smart as Shingo, 
who managed to show results

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.830
through his studies before he ran off.

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.360
I only managed to talk back

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:46.210
because I felt like he was insulting 
not just me, but my friend, too!

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.500
I could change thanks to my friends!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:53.880
When they've tried so hard
 and came up short,

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:55.760
I don't want them to be called failures.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:06.530
Yuugo, I'm sorry about the text.

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:08.420
Text? About what?

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:11.630
About your father saying the 
bacon you made was good.

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:13.730
I lied.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:15.830
Oh, that?

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:17.610
It's okay. No big deal.

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:20.340
When you're serious about something,

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:22.120
you wouldn't want to be lied to, right?

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:27.620
I kind of understand why you lied, though.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.030
Of course it'd make you happy

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:33.170
if someone said that what 
you made tasted great.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:35.600
You'd want that feedback.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:42.220
You sent that text because 
you wanted to hear it, too.

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:45.190
Are you the Hachiken-san who called?

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:46.130
Yes.

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:47.750
The train station, please.

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:53.560
But... please don't lie anymore.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:57.260
I can take anything now.

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:01.490
I'm not the same person I was before.

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:05.670
Okay.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:25.000
Mika...

00:19:30.470 --> 00:19:32.000
The clean-up's done?

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:34.230
Yeah. Brr...

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.220
Oh, are there fewer people now?

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:39.390
Everybody who doesn't live in 
dorms went home already.

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:42.510
Hey, Aikawa, are you going to leave 
the dorm once you're a second-year?

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:43.160
Yeah.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:45.190
I plan to find a place so 
that I can go to cram school.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:46.170
I see.

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.130
Wonder what I'll do.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:48.660
I'm gonna find a place, too!

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:50.120
I want a room to myself!

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.250
Me, too!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.510
I might stay in the dorm.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:54.790
I have to take care of the horses, after all.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.300
I might find a place.

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:58.080
<i>I see.</i>

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:01.350
<i>Dairy science students are forced 
to live in dorms their first year,</i>

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:04.180
<i>but most move out 
for their second year...</i>

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:09.930
<i>So I won't be spending every day and night 
with these guys for much longer.</i>

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.930
But getting your own place 
just to go to cram school?

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:14.390
That's weird!

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:16.680
You're studying hard, too, Aki.

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:19.070
Yeah, my great-granny told me

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:22.030
that if I'm going to do something I 
love, I should be serious about it.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.030
I see...

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:25.710
If I'm going to study cheese seriously...

00:20:25.710 --> 00:20:27.760
The real deal is in France.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:29.670
France...

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:31.120
France, huh?

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:34.040
Crap, I'm starting to lean in that direction.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.670
If you go, you'll really need to be ready.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:38.480
You don't know French, either.

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:40.420
There are distance learning seminars.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:42.340
I guess there's no harm in trying.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.900
Once you start thinking about it,

00:20:44.900 --> 00:20:47.350
the possibilities are pretty endless.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:48.310
Yeah.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:53.690
Maybe Hachiken-kun's dreams are 
endless from here on out.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.660
Snow...

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:08.730
Good job.

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:10.500
Here's your pay for today.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.010
Thank you.

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:13.580
They say this one's gonna stick.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:14.880
Be careful on your way home.

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:15.700
I will.

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:12.500
Oops.

00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:16.010
That angle was too steep!

00:22:16.010 --> 00:22:18.440
Take it slowly and give 
yourself enough room to turn.

00:22:19.030 --> 00:22:19.950
Okay!

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:25.440
Um, can I try that last jump again?

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:27.140
Oh, sure.

00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:27.980
Jump, jump.

00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:29.780
Keep jumping.

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:30.950
You go ahead.

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:31.800
Go.

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:32.530
Okay.

00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:34.690
You first.

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:36.960
Okay!

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:40.550
Here I go!

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:46.910
The End

00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:50.430
This story is a work of fiction.
